WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.434
-Daniel Humm, it is so good
to see you, buddy.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:07.133
You look fantastic.
Congrats on all this.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:10.467
-Thank you so much.
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.934
-You did it.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:13.701
You know, I have been
the biggest fan of

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:17.367
you and your restaurant,
eleven Madison, for a long time.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:22.234
And you became the
best restaurant in New York,

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:24.567
and then it was
best restaurant in the world,

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:27.868
and then you changed
your menu completely.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.934
Who does that?
And why would you do that?

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.300
What kind of
insane human being are you?

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.300
-You know,
I brought a little note

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.033
that's hanging in my office,
and it's right here.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.133
And it's a note
that deeply inspires me,

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:45.701
and it's by you
that you sent me in 2017.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.901
-Oh, my gosh. I kind of --
I remember this.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.067
Oh, yeah. I put...

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.033
Yeah.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.734
-So I've been trying to
figure out space.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.400
-Space.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.367
-But, dude, do you remember,
I -- Wow, I remember this,

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.367
'cause I was so happy for you
because you're just such

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:06.601
a brilliant guy, and everyone,
the whole crew over there --

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.501
By the way, it is an
out-of-this-world experience

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.300
to go to Eleven Madison.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.534
And it's just so well done,
top to bottom, everybody.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.133
Of course you're going to get
awarded a Michelin star.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.701
But how long has
Michelin been around?

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:23.734
-So, like, this award
that we just received --

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:27.467
it was three Michelin stars
for the first vegan restaurant

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.167
in history ever.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:32.734
So it was really meaningful,
because Michelin --

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.267
it's been around for over
100 years,

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.767
and they have sort of
written the rules

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:41.100
of what a
fine-dining restaurant is.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.734
Every chef
is sort of guided by that.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:47.834
And Eleven Madison Park had
three Michelin stars

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:52.534
for eleven years in a row,
but for serving meat.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.467
Our restaurant was famous for

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:59.601
honey-lavender duck
and poached lobsters and caviar.

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:01.634
-I remember,
when you changed over to vegan,

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.534
I go -- I mean, I love you,
but I'm like,

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.434
"Look, buddy,
I'm rooting for you,

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.667
but are people
going to buy this?"

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:12.267
I mean, people must have
thought you were crazy.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.067
-You know, I'm not going to lie,

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.100
but there were moments
that were really scary.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.567
Like, during the pandemic,
I spent a lot of time by myself

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.834
and so a lot in solitude.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.601
And I also realized that
the world is changing

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:29.367
and the food system is changing
and the climate is changing.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:32.400
And I felt like
I had a responsibility

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:39.968
to use this platform,
to use my voice of food

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.701
to speak
and to use my creativity

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:46.601
to make that future more
delicious and more beautiful.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.834
But as we got closer
to the reopening,

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.167
I was, like,
at home, couldn't sleep.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:54.100
I was like,
"Is anyone going to come?"

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.167
You know?
-Yeah.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.667
-It was scary.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.734
And I think,
with the Michelin award,

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:03.367
like with anything,
with a new album --

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.434
any artist, a new album,
a painting, or --

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.200
It's so much about being at
the right moment,

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.868
at, you know, the right time.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:15.200
And I think you can be
one step ahead,

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.000
but you can't be 10 steps ahead.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.667
And so with
this recognition of Michelin,

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:24.634
it just was really helpful
to create this forward momentum

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.000
for our team
and for everyone around it

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.734
that it was essential --

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.133
-You're in
the history books, bud.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:33.067
And, honestly,
I was so happy when I saw it.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:35.367
It was all over the Internet.
I was like, "Oh, my gosh!"

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.634
I texted you like,
"I'm freaking out right, bud.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.167
I'm freaking out.
It's is so cool."

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.701
And I think it's
changing the game.

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:42.834
It has to.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.300
-You know, in the beginning,
it felt like

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.100
I would leave
a lot behind, like,

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.234
leaving all these techniques
that I've learned for years,

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:52.100
perfected, and the
ingredients I've worked with.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.167
But then, what I found is, like,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.801
using plants
and vegetables to cook --

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:00.367
it's so liberating, it's
so beautiful, it's the future.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.701
And, in a way,
now I'm looking back

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.701
and I feel I was limited before,

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.501
because now we're
really cooking entirely --

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:11.067
We started our own farm,
called Magic Farm, upstate

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:13.701
and we're using most of
our ingredients from the farm.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.167
It's just been so beautiful.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:18.567
-But even the Eleven Madison
Home -- can we talk about this?

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:22.834
-So, we were here before and
we launched Eleven Madison Home,

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.234
and, at first, it was just
available for New York City,

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.634
and we just expanded to be
nationwide.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.367
It's elevenmadisonhome.com.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:35.868
And we have the kitchen
essentials, pantry items,

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:38.200
all the things we use
in the kitchen

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.334
to make things
more delicious and successful.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:44.367
But then we also, of course,
have our granola and our snacks

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.367
and peanut butter.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:50.033
But we really want to make
plant-based foods the future

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.167
and bring it into people's home,
and I think this is

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.100
a great way to have a taste
all over America.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.033
-Even if you just start
with one meal,

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.834
just do a little plant-based
and just slowly --

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.767
It's all helping the world.

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:04.033
-you know, this is not
anti-meat, but it is pro-planet.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:09.934
And I think one issue
I have is that we are so --

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:13.367
And I think it's about progress
and not perfection,

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:17.167
and sometimes, when people
don't do something 100%,

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:21.367
they get criticized, but change
happens from slowly changing.

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:23.834
You can't change one day
to the other.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:27.734
So I think if we all can just
reduce how much meat we eat,

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.834
we will have a better world
and a better climate.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:31.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.601
-I love you.
I'm so happy for you, bud.

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:39.834
Chef Daniel Humm, everybody.
Check out elevenmadisonhome.com.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:42.133
Cole Swindell performs after
the break. Stick around.

